2026-09-27T12:05:55.9199783Z Description:
2026-09-27T12:05:55.9200317Z This PPA contains more recent Python versions packaged for Ubuntu.
2026-09-27T12:05:55.9200678Z 
2026-09-27T12:05:55.9201457Z Disclaimer: there's no guarantee of timely updates in case of security problems or other issues. If you want to use them in a security-or-otherwise-critical environment (say, on a production server), you do so at your own risk.
2026-09-27T12:05:55.9202823Z 
2026-09-27T12:05:55.9202914Z Update Note
2026-09-27T12:05:55.9203104Z ===========
2026-09-27T12:05:55.9203378Z Please use this repository instead of ppa:fkrull/deadsnakes.
2026-09-27T12:05:55.9203644Z 
2026-09-27T12:05:55.9203729Z Reporting Issues
2026-09-27T12:05:55.9203949Z ================
2026-09-27T12:05:55.9204077Z 
2026-09-27T12:05:55.9204236Z Issues can be reported in the master issue tracker at:
2026-09-27T12:05:55.9204592Z https://github.com/deadsnakes/issues/issues
2026-09-27T12:05:55.9204798Z 
2026-09-27T12:05:55.9204910Z Supported Ubuntu and Python Versions
2026-09-27T12:05:55.9205173Z ====================================
2026-09-27T12:05:55.9205367Z 
2026-09-27T12:05:55.9205497Z - Ubuntu 22.04 (jammy) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.10)
2026-09-27T12:05:55.9205883Z - Ubuntu 24.04 (noble) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.12)
2026-09-27T12:05:55.9206221Z - Ubuntu 26.04 (resolute) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.14)
2026-09-27T12:05:55.9206867Z - Note: Python 3.10 (jammy), Python3.12 (noble), Python3.14 (resolute) are not provided by deadsnakes as upstream ubuntu provides those packages.
2026-09-27T12:05:55.9207377Z 
2026-09-27T12:05:55.9207483Z Why some packages aren't built:
2026-09-27T12:05:55.9207926Z - Note: for 22.04+, older python versions requre libssl<3 so they are not currently built
2026-09-27T12:05:55.9208448Z - If you need these, reach out to asottile to set up a private ppa
2026-09-27T12:05:55.9208719Z 
2026-09-27T12:05:55.9209006Z The packages may also work on other versions of Ubuntu or Debian, but that is not tested or supported.
2026-09-27T12:05:55.9209400Z 
2026-09-27T12:05:55.9209477Z Packages
2026-09-27T12:05:55.9209661Z ========
2026-09-27T12:05:55.9209777Z 
2026-09-27T12:05:55.9211018Z The packages provided here are loosely based on the debian upstream packages with some modifications to make them more usable as non-default pythons and on ubuntu.  As such, the packages follow debian's patterns and often do not include a full python distribution with just `apt install python#.#`.  Here is a list of packages that may be useful along with the default install:
2026-09-27T12:05:55.9212723Z 
2026-09-27T12:05:55.9212961Z - `python#.#-dev`: includes development headers for building C extensions
2026-09-27T12:05:55.9213425Z - `python#.#-venv`: provides the standard library `venv` module
2026-09-27T12:05:55.9214198Z - `python#.#-distutils`: provides the standard library `distutils` module
2026-09-27T12:05:55.9214787Z - `python#.#-lib2to3`: provides the `2to3-#.#` utility as well as the standard library `lib2to3` module
2026-09-27T12:05:55.9215342Z - `python#.#-gdbm`: provides the standard library `dbm.gnu` module
2026-09-27T12:05:55.9285255Z - `python#.#-tk`: provides the standard library `tkinter` module
2026-09-27T12:05:55.9286246Z 
2026-09-27T12:05:55.9286447Z Third-Party Python Modules
2026-09-27T12:05:55.9286946Z ==========================
2026-09-27T12:05:55.9287208Z 
2026-09-27T12:05:55.9288998Z Python modules in the official Ubuntu repositories are packaged to work with the Python interpreters from the official repositories. Accordingly, they generally won't work with the Python interpreters from this PPA. As an exception, pure-Python modules for Python 3 will work, but any compiled extension modules won't.
2026-09-27T12:05:55.9291028Z 
2026-09-27T12:05:55.9292527Z To install 3rd-party Python modules, you should use the common Python packaging tools.  For an introduction into the Python packaging ecosystem and its tools, refer to the Python Packaging User Guide:
2026-09-27T12:05:55.9294178Z https://packaging.python.org/installing/
2026-09-27T12:05:55.9294564Z 
